@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "ZapWatch";
}

<div class="zw-hero">
    <p class="zw-eyebrow mb-3">Silent-failure monitoring for Zapier</p>
    <h1 class="mb-3">Know the second a client automation goes quiet.</h1>
    <p class="lead mb-4">
        Zaps don't error out when they break — they just stop. ZapWatch watches for the ping
        that should follow every run and alerts you by email and SMS the moment one goes
        overdue, so you catch it before your client does.
    </p>
    <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        @if (User.Identity?.IsAuthenticated == true)
        {
            <a asp-controller="Automations" asp-action="Index" class="btn btn-primary">Go to your automations</a>
        }
        else
        {
            <a asp-controller="Account" asp-action="Register" class="btn btn-primary">Sign up</a>
            <a asp-controller="Account" asp-action="Login" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">Log in</a>
        }
    </div>
</div>

<div class="zw-flow">
    <div class="zw-flow-step">
        <span class="zw-flow-num">STEP 1</span>
        <h3>Register the automation</h3>
        <p>Name it, set how often it should run and how much grace to allow before it counts as overdue.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="zw-flow-step">
        <span class="zw-flow-num">STEP 2</span>
        <h3>Point a ping at it</h3>
        <p>Add a Webhooks by Zapier step to the end of the Zap, pointed at the unique ping URL ZapWatch gives you.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="zw-flow-step">
        <span class="zw-flow-num">STEP 3</span>
        <h3>Get alerted if it stops</h3>
        <p>Miss a window and you'll get an email + SMS right away. The next successful ping clears it automatically.</p>
    </div>
</div>
